WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.320
Fast and Furious 9 is no longer fast approaching
theaters and there's a chance fans will be

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:05.980
furious about it.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.180
"You think this is a joke?

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.320
Huh?"

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.720
As confirmed by Variety, Universal Pictures
has delayed the ninth Fast film by almost

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.920
a year amid concerns over the worldwide coronavirus
outbreak.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.939
It's the kind of thing that can make you want
to lean back, crack open a cold one, and wait

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.140
for it all to blow over.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.700
“You can have any brew you want -- as long
as it’s Corona.”

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.690
The studio's decision arose after consideration
about the consequences COVID-19 a new strain

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.400
of the coronavirus family of viruses that
originated in Wuhan, China at the end of 2019

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.140
has already had on the global economy and
what the continual spread of the disease will

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.720
do to the film industry at large.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.200
"One thing I can guarantee you, Dom — no
one's ready for this."

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.100
COVID-19 is, as of the making of this video,
most prominent in China, South Korea, and

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.120
Italy countries that have taken serious precautions
to keep their citizens safe.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.360
Such preventative measures include cancelling
public gatherings, issuing quarantine orders,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.540
and, of course, shutting down movie theaters.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.740
Many outlets are reporting that the United
States may follow the example of these overseas

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.220
territories with regard to theater closures.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.810
Noted Bloodsport fan President Trump even
evoked the action franchise, perhaps inadvertently,

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.320
while hosting the Irish Prime Minister on
March 12th ...

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.520
“When you think of what happened to Europe,
because it was very fast and very furious

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.040
Fast and Furious 9 was scheduled to open in
theaters on May 22, 2020.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.520
Now, it will arrive on cinema screens on April
2, 2021.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.160
International release dates are apparently
being ironed out, but the intention is to

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:36.420
launch the ninth Fast film worldwide in April
of next year.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.750
The cast and crew of F9 released a statement
on Twitter addressing the delay which read,

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.240
in part,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.060
"We feel all the love and the anticipation
you have for the next chapter in our saga.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.280
That's why it's especially tough to let you
know that we have to move the release date

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:48.780
of the film.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.600
It's become clear that it won't be possible
for all of our fans around the world to see

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.420
the film this May.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.020
While we know there is disappointment in having
to wait a little while longer, this move is

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.000
made with the safety of everyone as our foremost
consideration.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.600
Moving will allow our global family to experience
our new chapter together.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.620
We'll see you next spring."

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.000
Though it's completely understandable why
Universal Pictures has delayed F9, what feels

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.200
particularly disappointing about this development
is that Vin Diesel, who leads the franchise

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.731
as the racing aficionado Dom Toretto, recently
assured fans that the film's release date

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:18.540
wouldn't be changed.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.440
Diesel promised that F9 was sticking to its
planned May 22 release date.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.000
In an interview published March 7th, Diesel
said,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.880
"[I] won't fault anyone in the world for saying,
'You guys are stupid for releasing this movie

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.480
right now,' [but] we need movies now more
than ever.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.520
We're already in a very interesting time where
cinema and the cinematic experience is so

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.020
threatened.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.620
So, yes, put it on record we're going to show
up."

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.800
What's a double bummer about this situation
is that this isn't the first time F9 has suffered

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:43.720
a lengthy delay.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.260
the film was slated to hit theaters on April
19, 2019.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.660
However, when Universal prioritized the Fast
and Furious spin-off film Hobbs &amp; Shaw starring

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.770
Dwayne Johnson and Jason Statham over the
main franchise entry, F9 was pushed to April

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:01.320
10, 2020 before later settling into its May
22, 2020 slot.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.760
What's interesting about F9 being pushed back
almost an entire year from not its first or

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:10.530
second but third established release date
is that its new one is the exact date Universal

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.770
previously intended to release Fast and Furious
10, the installment meant to mark the end

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.080
of the core film franchise.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.480
With F9 now occupying that slot, what does
it mean for Fast 10?

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.740
“If we do this, we risk everything.”

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:28.060
The simple and sad answer is that the film
will undoubtedly be delayed as well, and probably

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.300
substantially at that.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.320
Production on the film has, of course, not
started yet, and it isn't as if it can begin

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.900
in the middle of a global health crisis.The
best case scenario is that filming on that

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.950
flick will probably begin sometime next year
which means that, accounting for the time

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.600
it takes to complete a movie in post-production,
the 10th Fast and Furious film will most likely

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.420
receive a spring 2022 release date.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.100
F9 getting hit with a delay of this caliber
is a bummer all around, but better safe than

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:53.600
sorry.

